records.qn_text:
(a) the year-wise number of international tourists who visited India during the last five years, along with their country of origin;
(b) the details of top ten source countries of foreign tourists, year-wise;
(c) the details of most visited tourist destinations and States/UTs by foreign tourists;
(d) whether Government has undertaken any study on changing tourist preferences, average duration of stay and expenditure patterns of foreign tourists; and
(e) the measures taken to enhance tourism infrastructure in destinations witnessing the highest international tourist footfall?

(a) whether Government has conducted any audit during the last twelve years to assess compliance by Ministries, Departments, PSUs, autonomous bodies and statutory institutions with the Public Records Act, 1993;
(b) if so, the details therefor;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor and the details of institutions found non-compliant, year-wise;
(d) whether any action has been initiated against officials for unauthorized destruction, loss or improper maintenance of records;
(e) the details of organizations that have complied with Public Records Act, 1993, year-wise; and
(f) whether Government proposes to publish a comprehensive compliance report and digitization status of public records maintained by all Central Government institutions?

(a) the details of revenue collected through indirect taxes, including GST, Union Excise Duties, Customs Duties and various Cesses, during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) whether Government has assessed the distributive impact of indirect taxation, wherein persons below the poverty line and low-income households pay the same indirect taxes as affluent consumers while purchasing goods and availing services;
(c) whether Government considers this equitable and proposes any mechanism, including targeted tax credits, direct benefit transfers or other compensatory measures, to offset the disproportionate indirect tax burden on economically weaker sections; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government will furnish, based on the latest Periodic Labour Force Survey (PLFS), the State-wise, district-wise and national details of employment, unemployment, labour force participation rate and worker population ratio;
(b) the category-wise number of persons employed in Government (Group A, B, C & D), Public Sector Undertakings, organised private sector, white-collar, blue-collar, gig and platform workers, self-employed, casual labourers and other informal occupations, along with the average monthly wages at the national, State and district levels; and
(c) the State-wise details of youth and educated unemployment and the measures taken to generate quality employment and reduce wage disparities across the country?

(a) State/UT-wise electricity allocated from the Central Generating Stations during the last five years, indicating the quantity allocated, supplied and the applicable tariff, year-wise;
(b) the States with the highest electricity consumption during the said period, along with their annual consumption;
(c) the criteria adopted by the Central Government for allocation of power from Central Generating Stations among the States;
(d) whether India exports electricity to neighbouring countries, if so, the country-wise details of electricity exported, revenue earned and the agreements governing such exports during the last five years; and
(e) the measures taken by Government to strengthen inter-State transmission infrastructure and regional energy security?

(a) State-wise/UT-wise sanctioned capacity and actual occupancy of prisons, along with the total number of inmates, during the last five years; 
(b) number of prisons operating beyond their sanctioned capacity and  extent of overcrowding therein; 
(c) details of financial assistance released by Union Government during the last five years for prison modernisation, infrastructure upgradation and construction of new prisons to address overcrowding; 
(d) whether Government has assessed the impact of overcrowding on prisoners' rights, health, legal aid and rehabilitation, if so, details thereof; and 
(e) the measures taken by Union Government, in coordination with the States, to ensure humane prison conditions?

(a) the number of startups registered under the Startup India initiative during the last five years, year-wise and sector-wise;
(b) the number of startups that have ceased operations during the same period and the reasons thereof, year-wise and sector-wise;
(c) the details of seed funding and other financial assistance provided by Government to startups, including State/UT-wise allocations;
(d) the number and details of startups that have attained unicorn status; and
(e) whether Government has assessed concerns that Indian startups are disproportionately concentrated in logistics and consumer-oriented sectors rather than deep-tech and innovation-driven domains, if so, the corrective measures proposed therefor?

(a) whether an Indian passport constitutes conclusive proof of Indian citizenship;
(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;
(c) the eligibility criteria and verification process for issuance of an Indian passport;
(d) whether acquisition of foreign citizenship automatically results in cessation of Indian citizenship and cancellation of the Indian passport and the procedure followed therefor;
(e) the process by which foreign nationals, acquiring Indian citizenship, become eligible for an Indian passport; and
(f) whether Government proposes to review India's citizenship and passport framework in the light of internationally accepted practices to strengthen transparency, verification and accountability?

vg

(a) the objectives and implementation framework of the PM SHRI scheme;
(b) the state-wise funds allocated and disbursed since its inception;
(c) whether States are required to sign an MoU and adopt any curriculum, syllabus or policy changes prescribed by the Central Government to join the scheme;
(d) whether Kerala has signed or withdrawn from PM SHRI, along with dates and details thereof; 
(e) the consequences, including financial implications, for States that do not join or withdraw from the scheme; and
(f) the consequences, if any, for States which withdrew from the PM SHRI scheme, including the impact on Central assistance for school education?

(a) whether Government has assessed the impact of persistent inflation on household expenditure, savings and purchasing power, particularly among low and middle-income families, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the retail inflation rate for essential food commodities during the last five years and the principal factors contributing to food inflation, year-wise;
(c) the fiscal measures, including tax reductions, duty rationalisation and subsidies, undertaken to reduce prices of essential commodities; and
(d) the outcome of such measures, indicating the extent of price moderation achieved and the mechanism for periodic review?

(a) the total amount collected by Public Sector Banks and Private Sector Banks separately during the last five years towards charges for non-maintenance of minimum balance, bank-wise and year-wise;
(b) the category-wise breakup of such charges, including minimum balance penalty, ATM charges, debit card charges and account maintenance fees;
(c) whether Government has assessed the impact of such charges on low-income accounts and Jan Dhan Account holders; and
(d) whether Government proposes to rationalise or regulate such charges to protect customers, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the current storage capacity and utilisation of Strategic Petroleum Reserves;
(b) the quantity released during emergencies during the last three years;
(c) the details thereof during the last three years, year-wise;
(d) the expenditure incurred on expansion; and
(e) the future expansion plans?

(a) the breakup of retail petrol and diesel prices indicating crude oil cost, refining, freight, dealer commission, Central taxes and State taxes;
(b) whether Government has assessed the impact of fuel prices on inflation; and
(c) the measures taken to stabilize retail fuel prices?

(a) whether Government proposes to institutionalise a National Ease of Living Index for all cities and districts to assess the quality of public services, infrastructure, environmental sustainability, safety, digital governance and citizen satisfaction;
(b) whether measurable performance indicators and periodic independent evaluations are proposed under the Index;
(c) whether Government proposes to link Central assistance and incentive grants to the performance of States and Urban Local Bodies under the Index; and
(d) the timeline for implementation, the nodal agency and whether Government will place annual district-wise rankings and performance reports in the public domain to promote transparency, accountability and competitive federalism?

(a) the total number of citizens registered on MyGov platform and the number of consultations, surveys and discussions conducted during the last five years;
(b) the number of citizens' suggestions that have been accepted and translated into Government policies, programmes or administrative actions, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government has evaluated the effectiveness and transparency of MyGov in ensuring meaningful public participation; and
(d) the measures taken to improve accountability by publishing action taken reports on citizens' recommendations and feedback received through the platform?

(a) the current status of semiconductor manufacturing in the country, including public and private investments made under Government initiatives;
(b) whether Government has assessed challenges relating to critical chemicals, raw materials, components and supply chains, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the present domestic demand and production capacity of semiconductors, along with projected demand over the next five years;
(d) whether global semiconductor market volatility has increased the prices of computers, mobile phones and other electronic devices in the country; and
(e) the measures taken to strengthen domestic manufacturing, ensure a level playing field, stabilise semiconductor prices and protect consumers?

(a) whether Government extended any diplomatic, humanitarian, consular or economic support to Iran during the recent war in the Persian gulf region;
(b) the details of high-level diplomatic engagements, humanitarian assistance and evacuation or relief measures undertaken for Indian nationals and affected civilians in Iran;
(c) whether any requests for assistance were received from Government of Iran and the response thereto; and
(d) the steps taken to safeguard India's strategic interests, including energy security, connectivity projects and bilateral cooperation with Iran during and after the war?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the effectiveness of Mission Mode Recruitment initiative in filling vacancies across Central Government Ministries, Departments and autonomous bodies;
(b) the number of sanctioned posts, vacancies identified and appointments made under the initiative during the last five years, Ministry-wise;
(c) whether Government has identified departments where vacancies continue to remain high despite the recruitment drive and the reasons therefor; and
(d) the measures proposed to ensure timely recruitment, reduce vacancies and improve efficiency in public service delivery?

(a) whether Government has taken note of the sharp increase in prices of essential commodities and consumer goods in the domestic market following recent international conflicts and disruptions in global supply chains;
(b) whether instances of hoarding, speculative trading and artificial shortages have contributed to the rise in prices;
(c) the steps taken by Government to control inflation, prevent hoarding and ensure adequate market supplies; and
(d) whether Government proposes any special measures to protect consumers, particularly low- and middle-income households, from the burden of rising prices?

(a) whether Government has taken note of severe waterlogging, urban flooding and landslides in several cities despite the delayed onset of the monsoon and the annual allocation of funds for pre-monsoon drainage desilting and dredging works;
(b) the details of funds allocated, released and utilised by Urban Local Bodies for such activities during the last three years;
(c) whether Government has assessed instances of underutilisation or delayed utilisation of these funds; and
(d) the corrective measures proposed to ensure timely execution, accountability and effective urban flood mitigation?

(a) the details of agreements, Memoranda of Understanding and other pacts signed between Government and Government of Israel during the recent visit of Indian Prime Minister, including their purposes;
(b) whether Government was aware of recent military attack on Iran the following day and if so, the details thereof; and
(c) what actions have been taken by Government to manage and de-escalate the situation in the Persian Gulf and protect India’s strategic, energy and citizen interests?

(a) the details of welfare schemes implemented for fishermen residing in the coastal regions of Kerala during the last three years;
(b) the funds allocated, released and utilised under such schemes, year-wise;
(c) whether Government has identified families affected by sea erosion, high tides and coastal flooding;
(d) the number of houses sanctioned, relocated or reconstructed for such affected persons; and
(e) the steps taken to ensure long-term coastal protection, livelihood security and climate-resilient rehabilitation for vulnerable fishing communities in the State?

(a) the details of faculty appointments made in various Schools and Centres of Jawaharlal Nehru University (JNU) during the last five years, School-wise/Centre-wise and year-wise;
(b) the number of vacancies notified, the number of candidates selected against each notified post and the category-wise details thereof;
(c) the highest educational qualifications and academic credentials of the selected candidates, post-wise;
(d) the Academic Performance Indicator (API) scores or equivalent evaluation scores secured by the selected candidates at the time of selection; and
(f) whether any complaints or representations regarding faculty appointments during the said period have been received and the action taken thereon?

(a) the norms prescribed by the University Grants Commission regarding remuneration payable to visiting faculty, guest faculty and assistant professors (contract basis) in Central universities;
(b) the prescribed teaching hours and workload for each of the above categories, including academic and administrative responsibilities;
(c) whether such faculty members are required to adhere to the same attendance hours, institutional duties and workload as permanent faculty;
(d) whether Government has received representations regarding disparities in pay and service conditions despite comparable workload; and
(e) the steps taken or proposed to be taken to ensure parity, transparency and fair service conditions for such faculty?

(a) whether Government has taken note that many smartphone manufacturers discontinue software and security updates after a few years, rendering devices dysfunctional and forcing consumers to purchase new phones prematurely; 
(b) whether it is a fact that certain software updates have caused technical defects such as green screen issues, battery drain and performance degradation;
(c) whether Government proposes to mandate a minimum period of software and security support for smartphones sold in India; 
(d) whether any mechanism exists to hold companies accountable for faulty updates and planned obsolescence; and
(e) whether compensation or replacement norms will be framed to protect affected consumers?

(a) whether Government has taken cognisance of the growing problem of excessive and unnecessary honking in urban areas and its impact on noise pollution and public health;
(b) the existing legal decibel limits prescribed for vehicle horns and the enforcement mechanism in place;
(c) whether any assessment has been conducted on compliance by vehicle manufacturers with prescribed horn standards;
(d) whether Government proposes stricter penalties for misuse of horns; and
(e) whether mandatory low-decibel or smart horn systems will be introduced to curb noise pollution at source?

(a) the total number of pending cases before District, State and National Consumer Disputes Redressal Commissions, State/UT-wise for the last five years;
(b) the details of sanctioned strength and existing vacancies of Presidents and Members in these Commissions;
(c) whether Government has taken note of delays caused by understaffing and inadequate infrastructure;
(d) the status of enforcement of orders passed by Consumer Commissions; and
(e) the steps taken or proposed to fill vacancies, strengthen infrastructure and ensure timely disposal and effective implementation of consumer protection orders?

(a) the number of ad-hoc and guest faculty presently engaged in Central Universities and other Centrally funded higher educational institutions, institution-wise and State-wise/UT-wise;
(b) the prescribed norms regarding remuneration, tenure and workload for such faculty and whether these are being uniformly implemented;
(c) whether cases have come to the notice of Government of ad-hoc and guest faculty being paid below norms, assigned workloads equivalent to regular faculty and continued for long periods without job security or benefits; and
(d) the steps taken to prevent exploitation, ensure fair remuneration and regulated workload and to fill regular teaching posts in a time-bound manner?

(a) the details of youth-centric welfare schemes and programmes implemented in Kerala during the last five years;
(b) the funds allocated, released and utilised for these schemes, year-wise;
(c) the number of youth beneficiaries covered, district-wise; and
(d) the major outcomes achieved under these initiatives?

(a) the total income generated by Indian Railways during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the break-up of income from major segments such as passenger ticketing, freight/cargo, parcel services, advertising, catering, station development and other non-fare revenue sources;
(c) the total expenditure incurred by Indian Railways during this period, segment-wise;
(d) the details of losses incurred in various sectors or services, including suburban, passenger and other loss-making routes or segments, year-wise; and
(e) the steps taken or proposed to improve revenue generation and reduce losses across different operational segments?

(a) whether Government is aware of the controversies and allegations of manipulation related to Television Rating Points (TRPs) by the Broadcast Audience Research Council (BARC) in recent years;
(b) if so, the details of complaints received and actions taken thereon;
(c) whether any inquiry, audit or independent investigation has been ordered into the functioning and methodology of BARC;
(d) if so, the findings thereof; and
(e) the steps proposed to ensure transparency, credibility and accountability in television audience measurement in the country?

SR

(a) the details of welfare policies, schemes and programmes implemented by the Ministry during the last five years to empower youth with disabilities or differently abled persons;
(b) the funds allocated, released and utilised under each such scheme, year-wise and State/UT-wise;
(c) the number of beneficiaries covered under these initiatives;
(d) the measures taken to ensure accessibility, skill development, employment opportunities and inclusion of differently abled youth in sports and youth development programmes; and
(e) whether any evaluation or impact assessment of these schemes has been conducted and if so, the findings thereof?

(a) the total amount of toll collected on National Highways and other toll roads in the country during the last five years, State-wise and toll-plaza-wise;
(b) what percentage of this collection was through FASTag and other electronic means;
(c) how much revenue was remitted to private concessionaires, NHAI and State Governments respectively;
(d) whether any audit or review has been conducted to assess leakages, over-charging or non-compliance with toll rules, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the steps being taken to ensure transparency, accountability and uniform toll policies across States?

(a) provide the details that has led to recent large-scale cancellations of IndiGo flights and the resulting congestion and chaos at several airports, which caused severe inconvenience to passengers; 
(b) the steps that were taken by Government and the DGCA to enforce passenger rights regarding timely information, refunds, compensation, food, accommodation, and alternate arrangements; 
(c) whether complaints were received from affected passengers, and if so, the number thereof; and
(d) whether accountability has been fixed on the airline, and regulatory measures that are being introduced to prevent such operational failures and protect passenger rights in the future?

(a) whether Government has taken note that many train coaches operating in Kerala are in a deteriorated condition, causing discomfort and safety concerns to passengers;
(b) whether the Ministry will provide the year of manufacture and present age of coaches attached to major trains running in Kerala, including Intercity, Parasuram, Venad, MEMU, Malabar, Raja Rani, Netravati and other key services;
(c) whether the Ministry proposes a time-bound plan to replace old coaches with modern, safer rolling stock; and
(d) whether accountability will be fixed for delays in coach replacement?

(a) the number of Indian citizens who have migrated abroad for employment and for higher education separately during the last three years, year-wise and country-wise;
(b) the major destination countries and sectors of employment and fields of study involved;
(c) the steps taken to regulate recruitment practices and prevent exploitation of Indian workers overseas;
(d) the measures to safeguard the interests and welfare of Indian students abroad; and
(e) whether any bilateral agreements or arrangements exist with host countries in this regard?

(a) whether the President of United Arab Emirates undertook an official visit to India recently;
(b) if so, the details of bilateral meetings held and the major issues discussed during the visit;
(c) the number and nature of agreements, Memoranda of Understanding or joint statements signed between the two countries, sector-wise;
(d) the steps taken to enhance cooperation between India and the UAE in the areas of trade and investment, energy security, infrastructure, defence, technology and cultural exchanges; and
(e) the expected impact of visit on India–UAE strategic partnership and on the welfare of Indian diaspora in the UAE?

(a) total number of teaching posts sanctioned, filled and lying vacant in Central Universities, Indian Institutes of Technology (IITs), National Institutes of Technology (NITs), Indian Institutes of Management (IIMs) and other Centrally Funded Higher Educational Institutions (CFHEIs), State-wise and institution-wise;
(b) the number of faculty currently appointed on ad-hoc, contractual, guest and temporary basis in these institutions, category-wise and institution-wise;
(c) the duration for which such ad-hoc, contract and guest faculty have been serving in these institutions, whether cases of engagement beyond prescribed tenure exist; and
(d) whether Government proposes to regularise long-serving ad-hoc and contract faculty and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government acknowledges that India is lagging behind global leaders in artificial intelligence research and innovation;
(b) the reasons for India’s slow progress in AI despite its large talent pool;
(c) the comparative position of India in global AI innovation indices during the last five years; and
(d) the steps proposed by Government  to bridge this technological gap?

(a) the procedures followed for handling, storage and disposal of nuclear waste generated in the country;
(b) the current capacity of nuclear waste storage facilities;
(c) whether any new facilities or technologies are being developed for long-term nuclear waste management; and
(d) the international best practices being adopted by Government in this regard?

(a) the total funds allocated to Kerala under various tribal development schemes during the last five years, scheme-wise and year-wise;
(b) the details of fund utilisation by the State Government, department-wise and scheme-wise;
(c) whether there has been any under-utilisation or lapse of funds; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and reasons for such under-utilisation?

(a) the details of lines of credit (LOCs) extended to foreign governments through EXIM Bank or other agencies during the last five years;
(b) the total amount sanctioned, disbursed and outstanding under these LOCs, year-wise and country-wise;
(c) the rate of interest and repayment terms applicable to these credit lines; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure timely repayment and minimise default risk?

(a) the total external investments, financial assistance, grants and aid extended by Government during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the details of such investment and assistance, country-wise and sector-wise;
(c) whether any criteria or policy framework is used to determine the eligibility of countries for such investments or aid; and
(d) the benefits accrued to India from these external financial engagements?

(a) whether Government is aware of the exponential rise in residential and commercial rents across metropolitan, urban and semi-urban cities;
(b) if so, the key factors identified by Government for such a steep rise;
(c) whether any studies or surveys have been commissioned by Government to assess the rent burden on middle-income, lower-income households, working professional and students; and
(d) the steps being taken to ensure affordability for tenants in major cities?

(a) the details of tourism projects sanctioned for Kerala during the last five years;
(b) the current status of each sanctioned project; 
(c) whether any new projects are under consideration during the current financial year;
(d) the funds allocated to Kerala under various tourism development schemes during the last five years;
(e) the year-wise and scheme-wise details of funds released; and
(f) the funds utilized by the State Government, along with the reasons for any under-utilization?

(a) whether Government has received complaints from vehicle owners regarding engine malfunction, corrosion or breakdowns allegedly linked to the increased ethanol blending in petrol (E20 readiness);
(b) if so, the details thereof and the response furnished and action taken by Government to resolve such complaints;
(c) whether the Ministry has conducted or published any assessment on the compatibility of older vehicles, particularly those manufactured before E20 standards, with higher ethanol-blended petrol, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether Government is considering the establishment of a grievance or compensation mechanism for vehicle owners who experienced mechanical failures attributed to the use of ethanol-blended petrol?

(a) whether Government intends to review the timeline for nationwide implementation of E20 fuel or consider a phased approach based on vehicle compatibility in view of the issues reported by vehicle users;
(b) the safety evaluations or stress-tests conducted to determine the impact of E20 fuel on critical vehicle components—such as fuel pumps, rubber seals, injectors and catalytic converters; and 
(c) whether any safety advisories have been issued to prevent accidents or mechanical failures in non-E20-compatible vehicles?

(a) whether Government has identified specific schemes or projects under Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation where funds remained unutilised for more than six months after release during the last three financial years;
(b) if so, the names of these schemes, along with the exact amount lying idle in each case;
(c) the details of funds allocated, released, and actually utilised under Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation from FY 2020–21 to FY 2024–25, year-wise; and
(d) the percentage of underutilisation for each year and each major scheme monitored by Government?

G

(a) whether Government would outline the sequence of diplomatic exchanges that led to the ceasefire agreement between India and Pakistan after operation sindoor;
(b) whether any specific role has been played by the U.S. President in brokering or influencing the agreement; and
(c) whether Parliament, main opposition leaders or relevant Standing Committees were consulted or briefed at any stage during the ceasefire negotiations given the national security implications?

(a) the details of the agreement/Memorandum of Understanding signed with the Government of Kerala regarding PM SHRI schools, including the date of signing, key provisions, and objectives;
(b) the details of funds committed, released, and utilised under the agreement signed with Kerala for PM SHRI schools;
(c) whether the Ministry has received any request from Government of Kerala to amend, annul, or withdraw the agreement;
(d) if such requests were received, what were the reasons cited by Government of Kerala for seeking changes; and
(e) the decision taken by the Ministry to this request of Government of Kerala?

(a) the latest details on India’s public debt position, including internal and external debt components, and outline the steps being taken to ensure long-term debt sustainability;
(b) whether rising interest payments are affecting social sector spending, the details thereof; 
(c) whether Government is  exploring alternative instruments such as longer tenure bonds or green bonds to reduce rollover risks; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of shell companies identified, struck off, or penalised in the last three years and the details of the measures taken to prevent their re-emergence;
(b)  whether a real-time data-verification system is being developed to prevent fake or duplicate director identities; and
(c) whether the Ministry has initiated any collaboration with enforcement agencies to track money laundering linked to shell entities?

(a) details of funds sanctioned, released and spent under Pradhan Mantri Jan Vikas Karyakram (PMJVK) district-wise during the last three years, and whether any delays have occurred in approval or release of sanctioned projects, detail thereof;
(b) the districts where the gap between funds sanctioned and funds actually spent is the highest, and  reasons for low utilisation in those districts; and
(c) whether any States or implementing agencies have been issued warnings or directions due to repeated delays in completing projects, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of communal violence incidents reported against minority communities in each State and Union Territory from 2022 to 2025;
(b) preventive and remedial measures taken by the Central Government in coordination with State Governments and law enforcement agencies to protect minority communities and maintain communal harmony;
(c) whether Government runs any nationwide programmes to promote communal harmony, and whether their impact has been assessed;
(d) compensation and rehabilitation provided to victims of communal violence in the same period; and
(e) the manner in which Government monitors and evaluates the effectiveness of its measures to safeguard rights of minority?

(a) whether the Ministry has considered the repeated public and local representatives’ demands for deployment of Vistadome coaches in trains operating towards Nilambur to promote tourism and enhance passenger experience on this scenic route;
(b) the current status of any proposals, approvals, or plans regarding attachment of Vistadome coaches on this line, including any feasibility studies or timelines for implementation; and
(c) the steps taken to assess passenger demand and potential tourism benefits of introducing Vistadome or luxury tourist coaches on the Nilambur–Shoranur route in line with similar initiatives in other parts of the country?

(a) the allocation and utilization, year-wise, State-wise for each sport separately such as football, cricket, athletics, volleyball, indigenous sports, etc, including Khelo India, Rajiv Gandhi Khel Abhiyan, Urban Sports Infrastructure Scheme (USIS);
(b) the details of major infrastructure projects, hostels, stadiums and league-specific spends by type of sport and district in the last eleven years;
(c) the current status of ongoing projects and reasons for underutilization or project delays, if any; and
(d) the audit findings and steps taken by Government to ensure optimal and equitable use of sports funds across all disciplines and regions in India?

(a) whether it is a fact that, there are increasing cases of illegal drug consumption being  reported among the youth across the country;
(b) if so, the actions taken by Government to control and contain such menace of drug abuse;
(c) whether Government is planning to conduct any study to have a deep and comprehensive understanding about the drug addiction amongst youth; and
(d) the details of drug cases reported amongst the youth in the country in the last three years, year-wise and State-wise?

b

(a) the measures of Government to combat discrimination faced by minority individuals in employment, housing, and access to public services, and manner in which the mechanisms for redressal are being strengthened to ensure fair, equitable opportunities;
(b) recognizing the economic disparities, particularly landlessness and higher poverty ratios among certain minority groups, specific programs being initiated to improve their economic conditions, including access to credit, formal sector employment, support for minority-owned businesses; and
(c) the steps taken to ensure adequate representation of minority communities in Government bodies, public services, decision-making processes, reflecting the constitutional principles of equality and inclusion?

(a) whether there are Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) in the country experiencing significant regulatory compliance challenges;
(b) if so, measures Government has implemented to reduce these compliance burdens for MSMEs;
(c) the data on new MSMEs registered across the country over the last five years, year-wise, State-wise and sector-wise;
(d) whether it is a fact that a substantial number of MSMEs in the country got closed due to significant increase in taxes imposed by Government; and
(e) the data on MSMEs that got closed in the country over the last five years, year-wise, State-wise, and sector-wise?

(a) the details of Aadhaar cards issued in the country in the last five years, State-wise, year-wise;
(b) the details of Blue Aadhaar cards issued in the country in the last five years, State-wise, year-wise; and
(c) the details of people who still do not possess an Aadhaar card in the country, the details thereof, State-wise?

(a) the present status of road construction of  National Highway 66 from Kasargode to Trivandrum;
(b) what aspects of road work has been completed;
(c) whether it is a fact that the road construction after Malappuram district towards southern Kerala has not made any significant improvement;
(c) if so, the reason for such delayed work in road construction in those areas; and
(d) by when is the road work expected to get completed, the details thereof?

SS

(a) whether it is a fact that, there is an increase in the attack against medical practitioners in hospitals;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the efforts made by Government to increase the safety and security of medical practitioners in the country?

(a) whether it is a fact that there is an exponential increase in rental housing or flat facility in major Metropolitan cities in the country;
(b) the details of average rent for various types of house and flat facilities in major Indian metropolitan facilities; and
(c) whether Government is planning for any policy for any rent ceiling act in urban housing in the Country?

(a) whether any enquiry committee have been constituted to enquire about the Ahmedabad Air India flight crash;
(b) if so, the details thereof and findings of the enquiry committee report; 
(c) the number of people who have lost their life due to the air crash, both people on board and people on the ground level in the accident area;
(d) whether Government have provided any compensation to the deceased and injured; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details and number of reserved passengers travelled in various classes and sector in Indian railways in the last five years;
(b) the details of different sectors that have the highest demand in passenger travel;
(c) the passenger demand vis-a-vis seat proportion in various high demand sectors in Indian railways;
(d) the list of highest fifteen sectors which have the most waiting list for passengers in various classes in the last five years, year-wise; and
(e) the details of action taken by Government to resolve the problem of growing demand for railway passengers in various sectors?

(a) the amount that ASI has received from selling entry tickets to various monuments in the last five years, year-wise and monument-wise;
(b) the monuments that have received the highest income through selling entry tickets in the last five years;
(c) the details of number of people who visited each ASI protected monument in the last five years, monument-wise and year-wise; and 
(d) the details of amount spent by ASI on each monument for conservation and development in the last five years,  year-wise and monument-wise?

(a) whether it is a fact that tomb of Mughal Emperor Aurangzeb Alamgir is an ASI protected monument;
(b) if so, whether this details have been mentioned in the ASI website or removed on the pretext of recent threats;
